TI  - Using Endobronchial Valves to Manage Pneumomediastinum.
PG  - e70167
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70167 [doi]
LID - e70167
AB  - Endobronchial valves have a variety of potential applications, from lung volume 
      reduction in patients with severe emphysema to closing cavities in those with 
      drug-resistant tuberculosis. This report presents two cases in which 
      endobronchial valves were effectively used to treat pneumomediastinum.
