TI  - Endobronchial treatment of emphysema with one-way valves.
PG  - 255-60, x
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2009.04.002 [doi]
AB  - Numerous endoscopic procedures have recently been studied and progressively 
      introduced in clinical practice to improve mechanics and function in patients who 
      have emphysema. Bronchoscopic lung volume reduction with one-way endobronchial 
      valves facilitates deflation of the most overinflated emphysematous parts of the 
      lung. These valves have been designed to control and redirect airflow by 
      preventing air from entering the target parenchymal area but allowing air and 
      mucus to exit. The preliminary results have shown that this procedure is safe and 
      effective at medium term in a selected group of patients.
