PMID- 32153005
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20210113
LR  - 20210113
IS  - 2543-6031 (Electronic)
IS  - 2451-4934 (Linking)
VI  - 88
IP  - 1
DP  - 2020
TI  - Treatment of persistent air leak with endobronchial valves.
PG  - 27-29
LID - 10.5603/ARM.a2020.0075 [doi]
AB  - Persistent pulmonary air leaks are usually treated conservatively with prolonged 
      thoracostomy tube drainage. In case this approach fails, surgical revision used 
      to be the only option. This case report describes the successful treatment of a 
      66-year old patient who developped a pulmonary air leak after cardiothoracic 
      surgery that persisted despite attempted surgical repair and talc pleurodesis. 
      The treatment was successfully completed with endobronchial valves thereby 
      demonstrating that treatment with endobronchial valves doesn't only represent an 
      alternative to surgery, but that it can also be successful in case surgical 
      intervention fails.
